Notice: You have Deployment → ReplicaSet → Pod (3 layers!)

What Happens If Your Pod Dies:
Copy# Kill the pod
kubectl delete pod my-app-5d4m8s-xxxxx
pod "my-app-5d4m8s-xxxxx" deleted

# Check pods immediately
kubectl get pods
NAME                     READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
my-app-5d4m8s-yyyyy      1/1     Running   0          2s

# A NEW POD WAS CREATED AUTOMATICALLY!
The Deployment says: "I want 1 replica of my-app running. You deleted it? I'm creating a new one!"

Real Example: Web Server
Copy# Create deployment
kubectl create deployment nginx-server --image=nginx

# Check it
kubectl get deployments
NAME            READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
nginx-server    1/1     1            1           10s

# Create a service to expose it
kubectl expose deployment nginx-server --port=80 --type=LoadBalancer

# Now it's accessible from outside!
# And if the pod crashes, Deployment restarts it automatically
